	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg7247"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174" title="View the profile of Delheru">Delheru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 104<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=788.msg7247#msg7247"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=788.msg7247#msg7247">Re:Laterz</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> April 24, 2004, 02:17:36 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Ah I was waiting for a post involving something about the current situation. I didn&#039;t personally want to start posting details for some reason, but I feel the server community should get at least some information :P<br /><br /><br />Rough Timeline of the excitement:<br />1. Eelyen calls for this and that, but seldom shows up himself. Fignutn runs vast majority of FoT raids (maybe even all?) &nbsp;and his group is the only one even really trying to progress through Ikkinz trials. Eelyen gives them insights about these trials (holy trinity is not needed, which was posted after I said it was not needed on these boards), but remains unflagged even to Kod&#039;Taz. Some people are irritated by this whole high and mighty thing and the constant &quot;my&quot; rhetoric.<br /><br />2. Kinladar calls for a vote of no confidence in Eelyen<br /><br />3. A vote for new guildleader is suggested and approved by the officers, and they start setting it up.<br /><br />4. Eelyen appears devastated and posts a sort of puppy eyed post about stepping down since he doesn&#039;t have the trust of HIS officers.<br /><br />5. Not surprisingly some members of the guild sympathize with him, since his martyrdom was fairly good. Basically some say the other officers are bit mean, which Eelyen takes to mean they think the other officers are wrong. They also feel Eelyen should run for leadership, since he does have significant backing still. Some people even guildremove (Deren).<br /><br />6. Eelyen rallies! The people are with him and he won&#039;t step down! He will run for leadership at the very least.<br /><br />7. Core members including 4 of the 5 people (if I understand correctly) flagged through Ikkinz trials (unsure if Cyprian is actually flagged) get a deal from Triton to get full membership if they xfer, and they decide to xfer realizing they won&#039;t get rid of Eelyen that easily.<br /><br />8. Eelyen goes for the motivational angle:<br />&quot;Inspiration for my guild.&quot;<br />&quot;I know this is a hard time. But be assured I refuse to let my guild fall. This was my dream and my vision when I started it nearly 2 years ago.&quot;<br /><br />9. &quot;my my my my my my my&quot; is the topic of the whole post, which annoys a great many people. It&#039;s the same old Eelyen. More than one poster scolds him for the stupid and self centered rhetoric.<br /><br />10. With much of the de facto authority of FoT now on Povar, Eelyen apparently believes he has enough support of those left, that an election is no longer necessary (even though the unofficial favourite Kinladar is still on RN, as are other prominent members such as Zenoflare).<br /><br />11. People that gave him sympathy originally scold him for this and hope he&#039;d let the election go ahead.<br /><br />12. Some ventrilo drama ensues, but we were busy in uqua and couldn&#039;t get very good real time commentary =(<br /><br />13. Eelyen realizes what he took for popular support was actually sympathy and respect (yes, respect, some might consider that surprising, but he has indeed done stuff for the guild in the past and deserves some for it).<br /><br />14. Eelyen decides to step down again.<br /><br />15. Guildleads are passed to Zenoflare.<br /><br /><br />This is the cliffhanger we were left at!<br /><br /><br /><br />That&#039;s the dramaish side. I left quite a bit out since it doesn&#039;t really reflect on the server that much.<br /><br />I feel it just shows how badly people handled things inside FoT. Eelyen obviously, but the palace revolution was also extremely clumsy IMHO. The goal of having a different leader than Eelyen might have been noble, since Eelyen indeed did not play enough... but it certainly came out badly to the members (you should have guessed Eelyen would do that).<br /><br />Anyway, tips for Eelyen:<br />1. I had some authority when I was like 10 (soccer and whatever) and I still remember dad telling me I&#039;d get everyone hating me if I talked of the team or its accomplishments as &quot;mine&quot;. The same lesson has been repeated to me as one of the most basic things of leadership in the military and all over education. I&#039;m amazed you have managed to miss it.<br /><br />In other words: STOP WITH THE STUPID &quot;MY&quot; SHIT. Your posts get quoted to #ascent for the hilarity value. One of your recent posts had like 15 sentences, and me/I/my was in every goddamn one of them. Seriously. I almost drown in my ego, but at least I have the brains not to flaunt that to people I don&#039;t even pay to endure the idiocy.<br /><br /><br />2. Let someone actually playing EQ lead. If you don&#039;t play enough, you are not the leader. I have always supported move of authority if I&#039;m not playing enough, and frankly you should too. At least I consider my authority to derive from the fact that I give a sense of accomplishment and fun to the members. If members are not having fun or advancing, my authority will and SHOULD diminish unless a SOE is clearly to blame (hi Uqua =)! ). This basically derives from a combination of charisma, organizational abilities, knowledge of the game and effort.<br /><br />Don&#039;t try to control things from behind the curtain. Dyvim tried it and failed, and frankly you lack his charisma.<br /><br />3. Never let someone else be further than you in content. If you are not on top of the content, there&#039;s no possible way your knowledge of the game is up to par with the true core of the guild. It eats away authority and that can come bite you in the ass, as I&#039;m sure you&#039;ve noticed.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: April 24, 2004, 02:19:59 pm by Delheru</i> &#187;
								</td>
